hints:
/cc @pohly (not sure who I should ping for this one, I assume this issue can lead to bugs in a lot of places)

/cc @michaelasp 

Note that the attempt to replace old-style `retry` methods seems to be stuck. Old methods were marked as deprecated, with no clear next step, and some of the replacement code didn't get merged:

NewExponentialBackoffManager was [deprecated in 1.27](https://github.com/kubernetes/apimachinery/commit/831cf05a7c4f839939a6c5e1e8bee238ddc6baac), suggesting to [pass the result](https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/util/wait#NewExponentialBackoffManager) of wait.Backoff{}.DelayWithReset().Timer() to wait.BackoffUntilinstead. But Timer() returns a Timer implementation, not the BackoffManager implementation that BackoffUntil needs.

Not directly related, but someone picking this up may consider also finishing that deprecation.

I think this is an overwrite bug here: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/b3d59873a4c49084bcfcbacba94cd5ecd5ed1fa9/staging/src/k8s.io/client-go/util/retry/util.go#L62

```go
// OnError allows the caller to retry fn in case the error returned by fn is retriable
// according to the provided function. backoff defines the maximum retries and the wait
// interval between two retries.
func OnError(backoff wait.Backoff, retriable func(error) bool, fn func() error) error {
	var lastErr error
	err := wait.ExponentialBackoff(backoff, func() (bool, error) {
		err := fn() // Context.Canceled
		switch {
		case err == nil:
			return true, nil
		case retriable(err):
			lastErr = err
			return false, nil
		default: // <- err is not retriable or nil err is still Context.Canceled
			return false, err
		}
	})
	if wait.Interrupted(err) { //<- LastErr is never set, so it's nil err = nil
		err = lastErr
	}
	return err // Return Nil
}
```

1. retriable(context.Canceled) is false because RetryOnConflict only considers Kubernetes conflict errors retriable.
2. The callback returns context.Canceled.
3. ExponentialBackoff returns context.Canceled directly when its condition returns an error.
4. wait.Interrupted(context.Canceled) is true.
5. lastErr was never assigned because assignment only occurs in the retriable branch.
6. err = lastErr changes context.Canceled into nil.

The fix should be something like this which sets the err based on the retry function provided. 

```go
func OnError(backoff wait.Backoff, retriable func(error) bool, fn func() error) error {
	var lastErr error

	err := wait.ExponentialBackoff(backoff, func() (bool, error) {
		err := fn()
		if err != nil {
			lastErr = err
		}

		switch {
		case err == nil:
			return true, nil
		case retriable(err):
			return false, nil
		default:
			return false, err
		}
	})

	if wait.Interrupted(err) && lastErr != nil {
		return lastErr
	}
	return err
}
```

Note: I used chatgpt for help root causing this. 

Hope this helps, sorry if just noise trying to dip my toe in OSS kubernetes.

